DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
1912::$$$message_0009_0000_0000$$$::I gaze at the pleasant blue sky.[lr]::
1913::$$$message_0009_0000_0001$$$::After a meal, nothing beats sitting on the porch and sipping some tea.[lr]::
1914::$$$message_0009_0000_0002$$$::Ordinary happiness is the best specifically because it's ordinary.::
1915::$$$message_0009_0001_0000$$$::"...So, I looked into it and there is a corresponding Servant and Master.[lr]::
1916::$$$message_0009_0001_0001$$$::The one who dropped out on the fourth day after the Holy Grail War began was Einzberns'[line len=2]"[wvs][sestop time=1000 nowait=true]::
1917::$$$message_0009_0002_0000$$$::"Hey, stop spacing out![lr]::
1918::$$$message_0009_0002_0001$$$::I went through the trouble of checking this out for you, so you'd better listen to my report!"[lr]::
1919::$$$message_0009_0002_0002$$$::"Huh? Uh, what? Tohsaka?"[lr]::
1920::$$$message_0009_0002_0003$$$::I'm confused for a moment.[lr]::
1921::$$$message_0009_0002_0004$$$::Suddenly, I realize that Tohsaka's sitting next to me.::
1922::$$$message_0009_0003_0000$$$::"Don't give me that... [cacheimage storage=凛私服14b(近)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服14b(近)]Did you hear a single thing I said?"[lr]::
1923::$$$message_0009_0003_0001$$$::It's a sincere and straightforward show of emotion from Tohsaka. How unusual for her.[lr]::
1924::$$$message_0009_0003_0002$$$::She's so mad that she's forgotten her family motto to always be elegant.::
1925::$$$message_0009_0004_0000$$$::"...Sorry. I wasn't listening.[lr]::
1926::$$$message_0009_0004_0001$$$::Why are you here, anyway?"[lr]::
1927::$$$message_0009_0004_0002$$$::Anxiety builds up within me, like I warped through time to this moment.[lr]::
1928::$$$message_0009_0004_0003$$$::I literally can't remember how long Tohsaka's been here.::
1929::$$$message_0009_0005_0000$$$::"...[wait canskip=0 time=500][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服11c(近)][say storage=emi0111_rin_0030 name=凛]Wait. You didn't even know I was back?"[lr]::
1930::$$$message_0009_0005_0001$$$::"D-[shock vmax=25 time=300 count=-3]don't be silly. I didn't space out [font italic=true]that[font italic=false] badly.[lr]::
1931::$$$message_0009_0005_0002$$$::I probably just didn't notice you when you came and sat down next to me. So I probably didn't notice you when you started talking to me, either."::
1932::$$$message_0009_0006_0000$$$::"That's pretty bad.[lr]::
1933::$$$message_0009_0006_0001$$$::...[chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=凛私服06c(近)]Oh well. You mentioned those weird dreams and that those four days were still bothering you. You must be tired, so I'll let it slide."[lr]::
1934::$$$message_0009_0006_0002$$$::"Ah... Sorry again. I'm a little scared right now. And, uh, I'm not really spacing out, so stop staring at me like that."::
1935::$$$message_0009_0007_0000$$$::"Ah. R-right. [cacheimage storage=凛私服13a(近)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服13a(近)]I guess I'm a little close."[lr]::
1936::$$$message_0009_0007_0001$$$::Tohsaka abruptly sits up straight.[lr]::
1937::$$$message_0009_0007_0002$$$::Until just now, she was practically falling over me.::
1938::$$$message_0009_0008_0000$$$::"...Then I'll start over from the beginning.[lr]::
1939::$$$message_0009_0008_0001$$$::About the four days you mentioned, I ran with the assumption that this was someone's wish on the Holy Grail.[lr]::
1940::$$$message_0009_0008_0002$$$::I think the key to finding out who this person is lies with the four-day rule."::
1941::$$$message_0009_0009_0000$$$::"At first, I thought that the Holy Grail was only recreating four days because of some inherent limitation, but if that was true, then it could just repeat a single day forever. I don't think it cares about being economical."::
1942::$$$message_0009_0010_0000$$$::"Yeah. The Holy Grail grants the wish of its owner[line len=2]its summoner. It wouldn't think about trying to save its own magical energy."[lr]::
1943::$$$message_0009_0010_0001$$$::"Right. So there's another reason it's limited to four days.[lr]::
1944::$$$message_0009_0010_0002$$$::The person who made a contract with it can only recreate four days of the war, for whatever reason.[lr]::
1945::$$$message_0009_0010_0003$$$::And the important thing here is that it isn't starting a war or continuing the old one. It's only reenacting them. Do you understand the significance of that, Emiya?"::
1946::$$$message_0009_0011_0000$$$::"...More or less.[lr]::
1947::$$$message_0009_0011_0001$$$::They experienced the Holy Grail War once, and they're recreating it, right?"::
1948::$$$message_0009_0012_0000$$$::"Well done. If you figured that out, then the rest is self-evident.[lr]::
1949::$$$message_0009_0012_0001$$$::The reason for only four days being recreated isn't because the Holy Grail lacks power.[lr]::
1950::$$$message_0009_0012_0002$$$::It's because the culprit has only ever experienced four days of the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
1951::$$$message_0009_0012_0003$$$::They dropped out on the fourth day, so they aren't able to recreate any more of the war."::
1952::$$$message_0009_0013_0000$$$::"Is this 'they' a Master who dropped out on the fourth day?[lr]::
1953::$$$message_0009_0013_0001$$$::But there wasn't anyone like that."::
1954::$$$message_0009_0014_0000$$$::"Not in our Holy Grail War, no.[lr]::
1955::$$$message_0009_0014_0001$$$::But when I checked the records of the previous wars, there was someone who withdrew on the fourth day..."[lr]::
1956::$$$message_0009_0014_0002$$$::"Eh? What do previous Holy Grail Wars have to do with this? Isn't it recreating our war, the fifth one?"::
1957::$$$message_0009_0015_0000$$$::"You'd think that, right?[lr]::
1958::$$$message_0009_0015_0001$$$::But it's a little different. This is just a metaphor, but I think that your four days are a blank script, and we're the actors.[lr]::
1959::$$$message_0009_0015_0002$$$::The actors are allowed to ad-lib because it's a blank script, but the runtime is fixed at four days..."[cacheimage storage=凛私服11c(近),凛私服16g(近)][wvs][playstop time=800 nowait=true][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服11c(近)][wait canskip=0 time=300][chgfg textoff=0 textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服16g(近)][wait canskip=0 time=300][se storage=se097.wav][clfg textoff=0 pos=all rule=走る感じ time=400]::
1960::$$$message_0009_0016_0000$$$::Tohsaka startles.[lr]::
1961::$$$message_0009_0016_0001$$$::"Tohsaka...?"[lr]::
1962::$$$message_0009_0016_0002$$$::"The Bounded Field just went off. Shirou, come with me. We have an uninvited guest."[wvs][se volume=30 storage=se037.wav][clfg textoff=0 pos=all rule=シャッター左から time=400]::
1963::$$$message_0009_0017_0000$$$::"...You're right. It's faint, but the alarm's going off. I'm surprised you sensed it before it went off..."[lr]::
1964::$$$message_0009_0017_0001$$$::I wonder if she's got a warning net set up around herself.[lr]::
1965::$$$message_0009_0017_0002$$$::That's worrying. It feels like Tohsaka's powered up ever since she went to London.::
1966::$$$message_0009_0018_0000$$$::I follow Tohsaka outside.[lr]::
1967::$$$message_0009_0018_0001$$$::"..."[wm canskip=0][lr]::
1968::$$$message_0009_0018_0002$$$::Without turning to me, she gestures with a finger to stay right behind her.[lr]::
1969::$$$message_0009_0018_0003$$$::I nod and prepare for conflict, staying just behind her.[lr]::
1970::$$$message_0009_0018_0004$$$::Tohsaka is looking at...[lr]::
1971::$$$message_0009_0018_0005$$$::...a woman whom I've never seen with the naked eye.::
1972::$$$message_0009_0019_0000$$$::"Hello. What business do you have here on this fine day, mage from the Mage's Association?"[lr]::
1973::$$$message_0009_0019_0001$$$::"That's what I'd like to know. I heard this was Kiritsugu Emiya's estate, so what are you doing here?[lr]::
1974::$$$message_0009_0019_0002$$$::...I did hear that he adopted a child..."::
1975::$$$message_0009_0020_0000$$$::"You want to see his son? He has nothing to do with you Association people. If you have a message for him, I can take it."::
1976::$$$message_0009_0021_0000$$$::Tohsaka's smile also contains flat denial. In response,[lr]::
1977::$$$message_0009_0021_0001$$$::"...I have no desire to fight you right now.[lr]::
1978::$$$message_0009_0021_0002$$$::But I will take action if you are needlessly aggressive. There are witnesses here, too. Deactivate your Magic Crest."[lr]::
1979::$$$message_0009_0021_0003$$$::The woman nonchalantly suppresses it.::
1980::$$$message_0009_0022_0000$$$::It seems Tohsaka had activated the Magic Crest on her left arm.[lr]::
1981::$$$message_0009_0022_0001$$$::Having someone see right through her backup plan just makes Tohsaka even more tense.::
1982::$$$message_0009_0023_0000$$$::...But Tohsaka's just as aware of how pointless it is.[lr]::
1983::$$$message_0009_0023_0001$$$::The woman before us has no intention of fighting, and I don't think this is some kind of trick.[lr]::
1984::$$$message_0009_0023_0002$$$::I know this because she's on a completely different level as a fighting mage.[lr]::
1985::$$$message_0009_0023_0003$$$::If she decided to fight, she could render us helpless without even needing to ambush us.::
1986::$$$message_0009_0024_0000$$$::"...I understand. You're just here to inspect us today, I take it?"[lr]::
1987::$$$message_0009_0024_0001$$$::"Yes. I didn't come to fight as a Master[cacheimage storage=バゼット右手グローブ01a(中)][wvl][line len=3][chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=バゼット右手グローブ01a(中)]Still, I'm unimpressed by your lack of caution. Why isn't Saber with you during the daytime?"::
1988::$$$message_0009_0025_0000$$$::"Saber isn't with us...?"[lr]::
1989::$$$message_0009_0025_0001$$$::Tohsaka sounds quizzical.[lr]::
1990::$$$message_0009_0025_0002$$$::"...I see. Since we are both alive, that means they haven't met each other yet... It looks like I'll have to make it brief."[lr]::
1991::$$$message_0009_0025_0003$$$::She mutters something to herself that's hard to catch.[lr]::
1992::$$$message_0009_0025_0004$$$::The woman is looking only at Tohsaka.::
1993::$$$message_0009_0026_0000$$$::...There are fundamental discrepancies in their conversation.[lr]::
1994::$$$message_0009_0026_0001$$$::Like the date, the Servants she mentions, and even the way she says Tohsaka's name.[lr]::
1995::$$$message_0009_0026_0002$$$::It's like there's a wrongness that you'd notice if you took one wrong step, but neither of them have realized it.[lr]::
1996::$$$message_0009_0026_0003$$$::It's a chilly, precarious balance.[lr]::
1997::$$$message_0009_0026_0004$$$::This miracle is like walking a tightrope over an abyss.::
1998::$$$message_0009_0027_0000$$$::Without saying anything, I watch it unfold.[lr]::
1999::$$$message_0009_0027_0001$$$::Tohsaka's often told me not to say anything I don't have to if an Association mage ever comes around.[lr]::
2000::$$$message_0009_0027_0002$$$::I gaze at the woman blankly, astonished even.[lr]::
2001::$$$message_0009_0027_0003$$$::The eighth Master who was never there, and who shouldn't exist.::
2002::$$$message_0009_0028_0000$$$::"...This doesn't make sense. Did you come here to appraise Kiritsugu Emiya's legacy? He was a freelance mage who didn't belong to the Association."[lr]::
2003::$$$message_0009_0028_0001$$$::"That isn't within my jurisdiction. I was just curious about the winner of the previous Holy Grail War.[lr]::
2004::$$$message_0009_0028_0002$$$::Doesn't that go for you, too? Aren't you visiting the Emiya residence to acquire the Holy Grail sleeping in this town?"::
2005::$$$message_0009_0029_0000$$$::"Huh...?"[lr]::
2006::$$$message_0009_0029_0001$$$::Tohsaka's doubt turns to certainty.[lr]::
2007::$$$message_0009_0029_0002$$$::It sounds like she's finally figured something out about the puzzling conversation.::
2008::$$$message_0009_0030_0000$$$::"...Hold on. Does the Association have the wrong idea about the Holy Grail?[lr]::
2009::$$$message_0009_0030_0001$$$::The Holy Grail War is over. The ritual failed on a grand scale this time, and the foundation to summon the Grail itself is gone.[lr]::
2010::$$$message_0009_0030_0002$$$::The Fuyuki Holy Grail War ended with the fifth run."::
2011::$$$message_0009_0031_0000$$$::How wonderfully balanced.[lr]::
2012::$$$message_0009_0031_0001$$$::But then she strays from the path.[lr]::
2013::$$$message_0009_0031_0002$$$::It's only natural. This tightrope can't go on forever.[lr]::
2014::$$$message_0009_0031_0003$$$::Why is this woman going to such lengths to pursue this, when she already knows the answer?::
2015::$$$message_0009_0032_0000$$$::"...I want to confirm something.[lr]::
2016::$$$message_0009_0032_0001$$$::Did you just say that the Fifth Holy Grail War already finished?"::
2017::$$$message_0009_0033_0000$$$::   I feel a sudden chill.[lr]::
2018::$$$message_0009_0033_0001$$$::The instant Tohsaka confirms, the mage's fist will shoot out at her.[lr]::
2019::$$$message_0009_0033_0002$$$::But she faces the naked hostility head-on, and nods.::
2020::$$$message_0009_0034_0000$$$::"Yes. That miracle will never be summoned here again.[lr]::
2021::$$$message_0009_0034_0001$$$::The Fifth Holy Grail War ended due to the illegal actions of Kirei Kotomine, the overseer sent by the Holy Church.[lr]::
2022::$$$message_0009_0034_0002$$$::Since his death, the Church has withdrawn from this land too, not just you Association types."[lr]::
2023::$$$message_0009_0034_0003$$$::"Kirei...Kotomine?"::
2024::$$$message_0009_0035_0000$$$::It drops.[lr]::
2025::$$$message_0009_0035_0001$$$::The woman had managed to keep her composure when she heard the absurd news that the Holy Grail War was over.[lr]::
2026::$$$message_0009_0035_0002$$$::But that one sentence...[lr]::
2027::$$$message_0009_0035_0003$$$::...has finally caused the iron mask to fall from her face.::
2028::$$$message_0009_0036_0000$$$::"[delay speed=200 canskip=0]Kotomine is...[wvl canskip=0 time=500]dead...?[delay speed=user]"[lr]::
2029::$$$message_0009_0036_0001$$$::"Yes. He's been dead for half a year. He was defeated by the victor of the Holy Grail War, Shirou Emiya."[lr]::
2030::$$$message_0009_0036_0002$$$::Tohsaka's eyes turn to me.::
2031::$$$message_0009_0037_0000$$$::"Shirou Emiya... I...I don't know of a Master by that name. No, this Holy Grail War can't have a victor...[cacheimage storage=バゼット03腕変えグローブa(中)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=バゼット03腕変えグローブa(中)] It can't be..."[lr]::
2032::$$$message_0009_0037_0001$$$::Unacceptable.[lr]::
2033::$$$message_0009_0037_0002$$$::Intolerable. Hatred blazes in the woman's eyes.[clfg textoff=0 pos=all time=300]::
2034::$$$message_0009_0038_0000$$$::It lasts a few seconds.[lr]::
2035::$$$message_0009_0038_0001$$$::Tohsaka takes a step between us.[lr]::
2036::$$$message_0009_0038_0002$$$::"Hey. Do you mind if I ask something I've been wondering for a while?[lr]::
2037::$$$message_0009_0038_0003$$$::...What happened to your arm?"[lr]::
2038::$$$message_0009_0038_0004$$$::That's an odd question.::
2039::$$$message_0009_0039_0000$$$::"...Huh?"[lr]::
2040::$$$message_0009_0039_0001$$$::There are two surprised voices.[lr]::
2041::$$$message_0009_0039_0002$$$::The woman touches her left arm with her right hand, as if she just remembered it was there. She looks completely dejected now.::
2042::$$$message_0009_0040_0000$$$::"Ah..."[lr]::
2043::$$$message_0009_0040_0001$$$::There isn't even time to stop her.[lr]::
2044::$$$message_0009_0040_0002$$$::She runs off as fast as her legs can carry her, looking as if she's just seen a ghost.[sestop time=2000 nowait=true][lr]::
2045::$$$message_0009_0040_0003$$$::If anything, [font italic=true]she[font italic=false] seemed more like a ghost to me.::
2046::$$$message_0009_0041_0000$$$::"...The Association must be shorthanded. I wonder if they forgot to tie up a loose end."[lr]::
2047::$$$message_0009_0041_0001$$$::I'm not sure if it just doesn't feel right to go after her, or if we're actively going to avoid doing so...[lr]::
2048::$$$message_0009_0041_0002$$$::Tohsaka turns to me. Like you'd expect in a movie or theater production, the line is obvious.::
2049::$$$message_0009_0042_0000$$$::"...Well, she probably won't be back for the time being.[lr]::
2050::$$$message_0009_0042_0001$$$::She seems kinda mentally unstable, but her skills are the real deal. She would've beaten us if we fought her alone, so consider us lucky that she just left on her own."::
2051::$$$message_0009_0043_0000$$$::"So, do you know her? I've never seen her before."[lr]::
2052::$$$message_0009_0043_0001$$$::"No, it's my first time meeting her, too."[lr]::
2053::$$$message_0009_0043_0002$$$::"Okay. She sure went out of her way to ignore you.[lr]::
2054::$$$message_0009_0043_0003$$$::She's a capable mage, but it's like she didn't even realize you're a mage, too."::
2055::$$$message_0009_0044_0000$$$::"No, it's more like she didn't even notice I was there."[lr]::
2056::$$$message_0009_0044_0001$$$::The difference in our power must be so great that I didn't even register on her radar. [shock vmax=20 time=600 count=-2]It really hammers home how much I still have to learn.::
2057::$$$message_0009_0045_0000$$$::"Still, that's tough. I'm sure she'll be your enemy.[lr]::
2058::$$$message_0009_0045_0001$$$::If you want to do something about her, then get Saber to help,"[lr]::
2059::$$$message_0009_0045_0002$$$::she warns.[lr]::
2060::$$$message_0009_0045_0003$$$::Tohsaka gives me a pointed glance, her earlier cheer nowhere to be found.::
2061::$$$message_0009_0046_0000$$$::"I'm not sure what you're trying to say.[lr]::
2062::$$$message_0009_0046_0001$$$::...You're telling me to go together with Saber if I were to fight her?"[lr]::
2063::$$$message_0009_0046_0002$$$::"Yeah. If that doesn't work, then ask Lancer. I bet he knows what she's up to."[lr]::
2064::$$$message_0009_0046_0003$$$::It only took one encounter.[lr]::
2065::$$$message_0009_0046_0004$$$::Tohsaka figured out what was going on after only a few minutes' conversation.[lr]::
2066::$$$message_0009_0046_0005$$$::But that's all.[lr]::
2067::$$$message_0009_0046_0006$$$::She neither offers nor recommends a solution.::
2068::$$$message_0009_0047_0000$$$::"I'm heading back home.[lr]::
2069::$$$message_0009_0047_0001$$$::...I'm going hands-off this time. If you want to solve this, then do it yourself."[lr]::
2070::$$$message_0009_0047_0002$$$::Tohsaka leaves me with that cold remark.::
2071::$$$message_0009_0048_0000$$$::"...She sure is kind..."[lr]::
2072::$$$message_0009_0048_0001$$$::I murmur for some reason.[lr]::
2073::$$$message_0009_0048_0002$$$::Tohsaka hasn't abandoned me.[lr]::
2074::$$$message_0009_0048_0003$$$::If anything, I feel like she's giving me the greatest concession she can. She's given me a chance.::
901972::$$$message_9009_0019_0000$$$::"Hello. What business do you have here on this fine day, mage from the Mage's Association?"[r]::�